A||||4||sdm1964||How do you remove the metal drip rails?||||7||
Z||000000||sdm1964||10-03-2000||06:07 AM||||I got me a 100.00 86 GT fastback this weekend. Pics will follow. Me and 2xses are doing a fastback convert to my 86 se.How do you remove the metal drip rails without bending them? i am sure there will be more questions to follow.<BR>tia||||reg||7
Z||000001||2xsess||10-03-2000||08:19 AM||||I'm tellin' ya...don't need no stinkin drip rails  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> j/k <P>Actually yes we need some advice here. <P>TIA<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tigger||10-03-2000||08:22 AM||||Start at the top near the sail panel and carefully pull the trim downward.  Don't pull with too much force, because when it starts to lets go you can bend it easy.  You don't need any tools, the trim is just pressed on.<P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tigger.gif">          <BR> <A HREF="mailto:RacingStripes@hotmail.com">RacingStripes@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||2xsess||10-03-2000||08:46 PM||||Thanks, So there isn't any screws or anything holding it on? I couldn't remember.<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT||||reg||1
